+## Congruence notation
+
+Math has its own shorthand for "these two numbers leave the same remainder": **congruence**, written with three bars instead of the usual two.
+
+<MathBox label="Congruence">
+
+$$17 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}$$
+
+Read as "$17$ is congruent to $2$, modulo $5$." It doesn't claim $17$ and $2$ are the same number — only that dividing either one by $5$ leaves the same remainder, so inside mod $5$ they behave identically.
 
 </MathBox>
 
